# Copy to .env.local. One project key serves both APIs.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# Model provider: openai | claude-cli | auto. This template pins openai, the target configuration
# (an unset MODEL_PROVIDER means auto). For local development without OpenAI credit, set
# MODEL_PROVIDER=auto in .env.local: auto uses OpenAI when OPENAI_API_KEY is set, retries a call
# with claude-cli when OpenAI answers 429 insufficient_quota (and then skips OpenAI for 5 minutes),
# and uses claude-cli when the key is blank and the claude binary is installed and logged in.
# claude-cli runs `claude -p` on your Claude subscription; it has no embeddings, so document search
# becomes lexical (SQLite FTS5/BM25).
MODEL_PROVIDER=openai
CLAUDE_CLI_BIN=claude
CLAUDE_CLI_MODEL=haiku
# Optional local ports and simulator address.
APP_PORT=3000
BANK_PORT=4001
BANK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4001
# Host allowlist against DNS rebinding: every page and API request whose Host header is not
# 127.0.0.1:APP_PORT, localhost:APP_PORT or one of these comma-separated entries gets 421
# "Unknown host.". Write each entry as the browser sends it: the name, plus :port when it is not 80
# or 443 (e.g. bank.example,staging.bank.example:8443). Behind a reverse proxy or a public name,
# list that name here; production does not refuse to start without it, it answers 421 instead
# (and logs one startup warning when this is empty or an entry has a scheme, path or bad port).
# ALLOWED_HOSTS is read per request; APP_PORT comes from the config, read once at load time.
# With APP_PORT=80 or 443 browsers omit the port from Host, so set ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost
# (and 127.0.0.1) to reach the app locally.
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Development-only defaults; the evaluator supplies its own values. With NODE_ENV=production
# (`npm start`, `next start`) the server refuses to start while any of these three is unset,
# shorter than 32 characters, built on one of these defaults or equal to another of the three;
# the log names the variables. Use three different values, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32` each.
BANK_SERVICE_SECRET=banana-local-service
BANK_ADMIN_SECRET=banana-local-admin
SESSION_SECRET=banana-local-session
# Demo persona selector (GET /api/people, POST /api/session): no authentication, anyone can become
# anyone, operators included. Unset, it is on outside production and off in production; 1 or true
# turns it on, any other value turns it off. With NODE_ENV=production the server refuses to start
# while it is on. Leave it unset unless you need to turn it off in development. Start the built
# server (`npm start`) with NODE_ENV unset: the default follows the runtime NODE_ENV, so a shell
# NODE_ENV=development turns it on and the production build refuses to start.
# DEMO_PERSONA_SWITCHER=
